8. Show only names and salaries, highest salary first, skipping first two and returning next three:

Atlas atlas-hlruvh-shard-0 [primary] hr> db.employees.find(
|   {},
|   { _id: 0, name: 1, salary: 1 }
| ).sort({ salary: -1 }).skip(2).limit(3)
[
  { name: 'Gopal', salary: 61000 },
  { name: 'Charan', salary: 58000 },
  { name: 'Deepa', salary: 50000 }
]
